Several small, purely mechanical Groovy patterns for interacting with the
Hubitat platform were adapted from the project below:

  - the internal self-hosted-HTTP-call pattern (an App fetching a resource
    from its own hub via `httpGet` to a local URL), including the port-8080
    convention for hub self-calls
  - the defensive HTTP response body reader (`readHttpBody`)
  - serving File Manager assets back out through an App's own routes, and
    the cache-header split between no-store responses and version-stamped
    immutable ones

